&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Us&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Cloudflare, we are on a mission to help build a better Internet. Today the company runs one of the world’s largest networks that powers millions of websites and other Internet properties for customers ranging from individual bloggers to SMBs to Fortune 500 companies. Cloudflare protects and accelerates any Internet application online without adding hardware, installing software, or changing a line of code. Internet properties powered by Cloudflare all have web traffic routed through its intelligent global network, which gets smarter with every request. As a result, they see significant improvement in performance and a decrease in spam and other attacks. Cloudflare was named to Entrepreneur Magazine’s Top Company Cultures list and ranked among the World’s Most Innovative Companies by Fast Company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Cloudflare, we’re not looking for people who wait for a polished roadmap; we’re looking for the builders who see the cracks in the Internet that everyone else has simply learned to live with. We value candidates who have the instinct to spot a &quot;normalized&quot; problem and the AI-native curiosity to create a solution using the latest tools. Our culture is built on iteration, leveraging AI to ship faster today to make it better tomorrow, while ensuring that every improvement, no matter how small, is shared across the team to lift everyone up. If you’re the type of person who values curiosity over bureaucracy, and that AI is a partner in solving tough problems to keep the Internet moving forward, you’ll fit right in.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will build and maintain Workday reporting solutions and partner with cross-functional teams to deliver scalable, high-impact reporting that supports business decision-making.&amp;nbsp; You will serve as a subject matter expert in Workday reporting, data governance, and workforce analytics. This role drives the design, development, and enhancement of advanced reporting solutions and dashboards that enable strategic HR decision-making across the enterprise. With a strong understanding of Workday data structures and business processes, you will play a critical role in improving data quality, automating reporting processes, and strengthening the organization’s HR analytics maturity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workday Report Development &amp;amp; Architecture:&lt;/strong&gt; Design, build, and optimize complex, enterprise-level Workday reports (Advanced, Matrix, Composite, Discovery Boards, Worksheets, and RaaS) incorporating complex calculated fields and query optimization across Core HR, Payroll, Compensation, Benefits, Talent, and Finance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Stakeholder Advisory:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as a trusted partner to HRBPs, COEs, and executive leaders, translating ambiguous business requirements into scalable reporting solutions and intuitive, self-service dashboards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Governance, Compliance &amp;amp; Security:&lt;/strong&gt; Ensure data accuracy, consistency, and strict system security/governance across Workday analytics, supporting audit, regulatory compliance, and external benchmarking requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process Automation &amp;amp; Continuous Improvement:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead initiatives to automate recurring workflows, leverage APIs/integrations to enrich reporting datasets, and stay current with Workday releases to continuously improve system capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documentation &amp;amp; Enablement:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop and maintain detailed documentation for reporting logic, calculated field methodologies, and data definitions; manage hypercare, implementation rollouts, and user adoption across technical levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership &amp;amp; Operational Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Mentor junior team members on reporting logic and best practices, conduct quality assurance reviews, and efficiently handle ad-hoc analytics and production troubleshooting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5–7+ years of experience in Workday Reporting, HR Analytics, or HRIS with increasing responsibility and complexity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced experience with Workday Report Writer, EIBs, Calculated Fields, worksheets, and dashboards; Workday PRISM or other advanced modules a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated expertise working with large HR data sets and creating scalable, automated reporting solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
