&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do: &lt;/strong&gt;(Describe role responsibilities here/max 6 bullets)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and grow a team of engineers building AI-powered developer tools, owning hiring, ramp-up, and career development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the technical direction for the product we’re shipping, partnering closely with staff-level engineers on architecture decisions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive down developer cycle time while raising the bar on correctness - making AI-assisted development both faster and more trustworthy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product and Design to shape the roadmap for an early-stage product, translating ambiguous problems into shippable scope&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish the execution rhythm for your team: planning, delivery, quality, and operational ownership of the services you build&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are: &lt;/strong&gt;(Describe role qualifications here/max 6 bullets)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re actively shipping code with AI agents in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You thrive in early-stage environments where the roadmap shifts and the right answer isn&#39;t known yet.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a genuine point of view on AI coding tools - where they help today, where they fall short, and what it would take to close the gap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong technical depth in full-stack development (TypeScript/React and systems-level work) and stay close enough to the code to earn the trust of senior engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve built developer-facing products or tooling where speed, reliability, and developer experience were hard requirements&lt;/li&gt;
