&lt;li&gt;Experience in a customer-facing technical role such as Software Engineer, Solutions Engineer, Technical Consultant, Sales Engineer, Developer Advocate, or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of modern software development practices, including source control, local development environments, deployment workflows, debugging, and build tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to partner with enterprise customers to solve complex technical challenges and drive successful product implementations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to engage both technical and non-technical audiences across cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to thrive in ambiguous environments by creating scalable processes, collaborating across teams, and leveraging emerging technologies such as AI and modern developer workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;While it’s not required, it’s an added plus if you also have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong familiarity with developer, design, collaboration, or AI products, particularly those that connect design and engineering workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success partnering with enterprise customers on implementation, onboarding, migrations, technical enablement, and product adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of modern engineering practices, including frontend development, design systems, component libraries, CI/CD pipelines, monorepos, and Dev Infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to build, scale, or launch customer-facing technical functions, pilot programs, services, or engineering practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate customer insights and deployment trends into product strategy, documentation, roadmap recommendations, and engineering priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
