&lt;p&gt;As Area Vice President, you&#39;ll lead GitLab&#39;s Financial Services sales organization and shape how we win new customers, expand existing relationships, and deliver predictable growth. You&#39;ll build and develop a team of Regional Sales Directors who lead Enterprise and Commercial Account Executives, helping financial services customers improve how they build, secure, and deliver software with GitLab&#39;s DevSecOps platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Vice President of Sales, AMER, you&#39;ll set the strategy for the area while staying close to customers, leaders, and day-to-day execution. This is an opportunity to build a high-performing sales organization, strengthen key customer and partner relationships, and work across GitLab to create lasting customer value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Establish and deliver a strategy to win new customers, expand existing accounts with purpose, and create a shared vision for long-term growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Drive customer success and predictable year-over-year annual recurring revenue growth for GitLab.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Recruit, develop, and retain a diverse and effective sales organization of Regional Sales Directors and Strategic Account Executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;4&quot;&gt;Build and maintain key customer relationships, and develop strategies that expand GitLab&#39;s customer base in Financial Services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;5&quot;&gt;Provide detailed and accurate sales forecasts, manage the overall sales process, and set clear metrics for sales funnel management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;6&quot;&gt;Lead at both the strategic and operational levels, translating priorities into consistent execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;7&quot;&gt;Partner with Marketing, Channel, Alliances, Product, Engineering, and other teams to support customer outcomes and growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Progressive second-line leadership experience leading teams in strategic sales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Repeatable success recruiting, hiring, developing, and retaining leaders and individual contributors in a high-performing enterprise sales organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Deep experience selling into accounts in core Financial Services markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;4&quot;&gt;Consistent overachievement against an annual quota.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;5&quot;&gt;Progressive experience in software sales, preferably with development tools or open source software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;6&quot;&gt;A proven record of working closely with channel partners and cross-functional peers to support growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;7&quot;&gt;High integrity, initiative, sound judgment, and the ability to communicate and present clearly to a range of audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;8&quot;&gt;The ability to adapt, work independently, collaborate effectively, manage an ambitious workload, and learn and use GitLab.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;9&quot;&gt;A bachelor&#39;s degree and the ability to travel as needed in line with GitLab&#39;s travel policy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Financial Services Sales team helps customers use GitLab to improve how they build, secure, and deliver software. You&#39;ll lead through Regional Sales Directors and Strategic Account Executives, working across GitLab to build lasting customer relationships, support customer success, and deliver predictable growth.&lt;/p&gt;
