&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build and retain engineering talent in NYC, Boston, and Paris, mentor Engineering Managers toward Director readiness, and participate in the on-call rotation&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You have directly managed Engineering Managers, not just individual contributors&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You have deep experience with one or more cloud providers, ideally with experience operating large-scale systems in the cloud.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You have a solid understanding of cloud economics, as well as how to balance performance and cost in cloud computing environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You integrate AI deeply into how you lead and how your teams build, treating AI-first thinking as core engineering practice rather than a feature bolted onto the product&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You have a track record of shaping product decisions, not just executing against a spec&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You have worked with large-scale, event-driven or data-intensive backend systems — ingestion pipelines, high-throughput APIs, or time-series/event data at scale&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are&amp;nbsp; comfortable operating in English in a cross-Atlantic org, and are based in New York, Boston, or Paris.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;Datadog values people from all walks of life. We understand not everyone will meet all the above qualifications on day one. That&#39;s okay. If you&#39;re passionate about technology and want to grow your skills, we encourage you to apply.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
