&lt;p&gt;PhonePe&#39;s Data Platform powers India&#39;s largest consumer payments app at national scale—managing petabyte-scale infrastructure, batch/real-time pipelines, and developer tooling entirely on-premise. You&#39;ll build the core data infrastructure, tools, and internal products that enable hundreds of engineers, analysts, data scientists, and business teams to move faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Own product strategy&lt;/strong&gt;, specs, and roadmaps for data platform components, APIs, and developer tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Synthesize requirements&lt;/strong&gt; from business/product teams and translate them into system APIs, developer interfaces, and platform capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Work with architects&lt;/strong&gt; and engineering leads to balance reliability, performance, technical debt, and new features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Design solutions&lt;/strong&gt; for data quality, governance, cataloging, and pipeline efficiency at petabyte scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Define and track platform health metrics&lt;/strong&gt;: latency, query performance, uptime, adoption, resource efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Must Haves:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product Management Experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1-3 year as PM/APM with product ownership, OR&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2-3 years as Data/Backend Engineer with PM work (PRDs, roadmaps, user research)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Stack Depth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding: ETL/ELT pipelines, data warehousing, data lakes/lakehouses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced SQL (query optimization, not just SELECT statements)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on with ONE of: Hive/Spark/Hadoop/HDFS, Snowflake/Databricks/BigQuery, or Airflow/DBT/Kafka/Trino&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understands how data systems work end-to-end (not just BI layer)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Problem-First Thinking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Asks clarifying questions before solutions (WHO, WHAT, WHEN, WHY, HOW)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Articulates problems → solutions → outcomes (not feature lists)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesizes requirements from diverse stakeholders into clear product specs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structured Approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Breaks down ambiguous problems systematically&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;States assumptions explicitly and validates them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thinks in MVP phases and iterations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Holds technical discussions with engineers/architects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translates business needs into system specs, APIs, and developer interfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Writes clear PRDs, specs, and documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Good To Haves:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;TB/PB-scale data systems experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;On-prem stack: Hive, Spark, HDFS, Hadoop, Impala (cloud experience acceptable if fundamentals strong)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Built internal developer tools, APIs, or self-service platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data governance: cataloging, lineage, access controls, metadata management, observability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-native workflow: Active user of ChatGPT/Claude/GitHub Copilot; bonus for GenAI features (RAG, LLM apps)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High-potential signals: Published work, side projects, led cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
