&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Senior Manager, Channels – Brazil&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;As the &lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Senior Manager, Channels – Brazil&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;, you will lead Datadog’s Channel organization in Brazil, managing a team of Partner Managers responsible for building and scaling a highly productive partner ecosystem across the country.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;You and your team will recruit, develop, and manage Datadog Sales &amp;amp; Services partners, including system integrators, managed service providers, resellers, and specialized technology partners. You will be accountable for increasing partner-sourced pipeline, driving incremental revenue, strengthening partner capabilities, and ensuring strong alignment between the partner ecosystem and Datadog’s Sales organization across Enterprise, Mid-Market, and Commercial segments.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The role reports to the &lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Head of Channels &amp;amp; Alliances, Latin America&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; and works closely with Brazil Sales leadership, Partner Solutions, Marketing, Customer Success, Alliances, Operations, Finance, and Legal to grow and scale Datadog’s Channel business in Brazil.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead, develop, and manage the Brazil Partner Manager team&lt;/strong&gt;, setting clear priorities, coaching for performance, and developing talent.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the Channel strategy and execution for Brazil&lt;/strong&gt;, aligning partner coverage, capabilities, and investments with the priorities of the Brazil Sales organization.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Drive &lt;strong&gt;partner-sourced pipeline and incremental revenue&lt;/strong&gt; by increasing the productivity of existing partners and developing new partners where strategic coverage or capability gaps exist.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Build and maintain a balanced partner ecosystem across &lt;strong&gt;system integrators, MSPs, resellers, and specialized partners&lt;/strong&gt;, with clear segmentation and development plans.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Partner closely with &lt;strong&gt;Enterprise, Mid-Market, and Commercial Sales leadership in Brazil&lt;/strong&gt; to define joint account strategies, improve partner engagement, and increase partner contribution across new-logo and expansion opportunities.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Establish senior and executive relationships with key Brazil partners and serve as an escalation point for complex partner, commercial, and go-to-market matters.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Work with Partner Solutions to strengthen partner technical capabilities, certifications, services capacity, and ability to independently support customer opportunities.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Collaborate with the Alliances organization to connect Brazil Channel partners with AWS, Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud where joint go-to-market motions can accelerate growth.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Drive consistent operating cadences with the team and strategic partners, including business planning, pipeline reviews, account mapping, and performance reviews.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Own Brazil Channel metrics, forecasting, pipeline visibility, and reporting to Brazil and LATAM leadership.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Identify gaps in partner coverage, skills, specialization, or geographic reach and develop plans to address them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Who You Are&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5+ years of people leadership experience&lt;/strong&gt;, including hiring, coaching, and developing sales or partner professionals.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;10+ years of experience in Channels, Partnerships, Business Development, or enterprise technology sales&lt;/strong&gt;, preferably within SaaS, cloud, cybersecurity, observability, or related technology markets.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Proven experience building and scaling partner ecosystems and generating measurable &lt;strong&gt;pipeline and revenue through partners&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Strong knowledge of the &lt;strong&gt;Brazilian technology and partner ecosystem&lt;/strong&gt;, including system integrators, resellers, MSPs, and cloud-focused partners.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Experience working closely with direct Sales organizations across multiple segments, ideally including Enterprise and Commercial.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Strong business acumen and experience managing pipeline, forecasting, partner performance, and investment priorities.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ability to understand technical concepts and connect partner capabilities to customer and sales requirements.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Strong executive presence and ability to build trusted relationships with senior internal stakeholders and partner executives.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Based in São Paulo, Brazil, with the ability to work from Datadog’s São Paulo office as part of our hybrid workplace model.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills in &lt;strong&gt;Portuguese and English&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Comfortable operating in a fast-growing environment that requires both strategic leadership and hands-on execution.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
