&lt;p&gt;Datadog&#39;s brand is entering a new chapter, and we&#39;re looking for a Principal, Brand Editorial to own and evolve how we sound. As the founding writer on a multidisciplinary team of designers, illustrators, motion artists, and producers, you&#39;ll shape the ideas and narratives that define how Datadog shows up in the world. You&#39;ll also build the systems, standards, and tools that help thousands of colleagues scale brand voice and the company. You&#39;ll go deep on how the products actually work, then turn that complexity into clear, powerful ideas. You&#39;ll pair exceptional craft with real conceptual ambition, and raise the bar on both.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Datadog, we place value in our office culture - the relationships and collaboration it builds and the creativity it brings to the table. We operate as a hybrid workplace to ensure our Datadogs can create a work-life harmony that best fits them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and evolve Datadog&#39;s writing style, tone, and point of view, setting a consistent quality bar across campaigns, events, web, video, social, product marketing, and other brand experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Concept and write high-impact brand work, including campaigns, videos, launches, and major event experiences, as well as ongoing work across social, web, and sales enablement.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build practical voice and messaging systems, including style guidance, messaging frameworks, and writing standards that teams can apply confidently in their day-to-day work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Encode Datadog&#39;s voice into AI-enabled writing workflows by designing prompts, custom skills, evaluation approaches, and guardrails that help teams create and improve on-brand drafts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner early with Brand, Creative, Product Marketing, Web, Corporate Communications, and other teams to establish messaging before execution and strengthen briefs, concepts, critiques, and production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scale writing quality beyond your own output by coaching internal partners and enabling agencies and contractors to apply Datadog&#39;s voice consistently without creating a bottleneck.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 8+ years of writing experience and a portfolio demonstrating range across brand campaigns, voice or messaging systems, long-form storytelling, and concise creative copy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have written for developer, technical, or enterprise audiences and can communicate complex technology clearly without losing the substance that matters to practitioners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have built or substantially shaped voice guidelines, messaging frameworks, or writing standards that other people have successfully used.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a hands-on creative leader who can establish direction, exercise strong editorial judgment, influence partners, and carry work through production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You build with AI, not just around it. You&#39;re technology curious, you stay on top of modern workflows, and you have experience turning your writing standards into tools an entire organization can scale with.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable working through ambiguity, collaborating across functions, sharing your craft generously, and helping an evolving brand and its teams become stronger communicators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Datadog values people from all walks of life. We understand not everyone will meet all the above qualifications on day one. That&#39;s okay. If you’re passionate about technology and want to grow your skills, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
