&lt;p&gt;The Strategic Finance team is focused on solving some of Figma&#39;s most pressing business issues. The team is responsible for owning the company&#39;s budget, driving annual and quarterly planning processes, allocating and deploying the company&#39;s resources efficiently, performing financial analyses, and partnering with teams across the company. The role requires someone who is highly analytical and strategic, a great communicator, approaches problems in a structured manner, and is comfortable with ambiguity. You&#39;ll get substantial visibility, focus on the highest-priority business issues, and be plugged into every facet of the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full time role that can be held from one of our US hubs (SF / NY) or remotely in the United States.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do at Figma:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead all ARR (Annual Recurring Revenue) planning and forecasting for Figma&#39;s Self-Serve business, including annual plans, quarterly forecasts, monthly reporting, and weekly performance reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with Product and Data Science to identify key growth drivers, surface insights, and influence strategic decisions across the self-serve funnel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement process improvements that enhance forecast accuracy and improve visibility into customer behavior, monetization, and conversion trends&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and mentor a high-performing team—providing strategic direction, career development support, and hands-on collaboration to drive team impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and present actionable insights and recommendations to senior leadership, including the CFO, CEO, and CMO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and evolve the financial narrative for Figma&#39;s self-serve motion in executive and board-level materials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring a builder&#39;s mindset to scaling the Self-Serve Finance function—identifying tools, metrics, and systems that enable better decision-making at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&#39;d love to hear from you if you have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in investment banking, private equity, strategic finance, business operations, or a related analytical field, including 2+ years leading and developing high-performing teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in SQL and a history of partnering with Data Science teams to solve complex analytical problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience in financial planning, forecasting, and driving insights through data-driven analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A structured, strategic thinker who can break down ambiguous problems and develop clear, actionable solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of building new processes or scaling existing ones to improve efficiency and decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
