&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the Finance support to go-to-market (GTM) teams which could include Customer Success (CS) and Sales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support annual planning for headcount, T&amp;amp;E, and discretionary spending for GTM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet regularly with the departments to understand budget vs. actual tracking and calibration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain bookings forecasts and pipeline analyses for renewals and expansion, and flag risks and upside to leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze CS performance, including ARR, net and gross revenue retention, churn, expansion attainment, CSM productivity, and book-of-business coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Strategy team to ensure alignment of metrics and reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a strategic contributor (in partnership with Strategy) on decisions around CS account coverage models, account segmentation, compensation planning (and resulting expenses), and other strategic decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work as a part of the broader FP&amp;amp;A team to understand the company’s financials, analytics, and help the organization scale thoughtfully&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of professional experience in FP&amp;amp;A / Strategic Finance, Corporate Finance, Investment Banking, and/or other related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in finance, accounting, business, or economics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mastery of Excel and PowerPoint with proven experience in building financial models and managing complex data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a clear, concise communicator and team player with a humble mindset and ‘can-do’ attitude&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
